author alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790159791 +0400
committer alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790159791 +0400

fix(estate): the root Store sidecar id is the protocol constant "store"

A new estate's ceremony approved the Store's Foundation Global under
`${rootStoreId}-v2`, while the Store boots with "store"
(estate_store_config_render.go BootIdentity.SidecarID, boot-identity-prep
default), the deployer's Foundation manifest has a `store` row
(config/global-sidecars.tsv, SAN store.sidecar.host), and both repositories'
estateprofile/store_enrollment.go forbid deriving the id from StoreID.
register_sidecar_identity reads the Global, Reseller and Local approvals under
the id it seeds the identity with, so the Store's identity registration would
have found its Global uninitialized. `-v2` is the retiring estate's rotation
label; that estate's own tooling keeps its pins.

- profile.mjs: export ROOT_STORE_SIDECAR_ID = 'store'; ceremonySidecarId
  returns it. The 29-byte rootStoreId cap (which existed only because the id
  was folded into a seed) is replaced by a SAN/id agreement check: every
  ceremony SAN must be <id>.sidecar.{host,hypervisor,local,remote}.
- closure.mjs: the Store tree's sidecar pins call ceremonySidecarId instead
  of a second, independent `${storeId}-v2` derivation.
- plan.mjs: ApproveGlobalSidecar is init-only, so the root Store's Global is
  ONE step (approve-root-store-sidecar, the executor's approve-global-sidecar
  with the profile's values), and the manifest step runs after it and
  excludes the `store` row (the emitter skips a row only when its PDA exists).
- chain-ix.mjs: reseller/local sidecar and sidecar_identity PDAs; key_version
  is refused unless it is a u32 (writeUInt32LE truncates a fraction).
- testdata/sidecar-pda-vectors.json: cross-language vector (fixed synthetic
  program/mints, id "store", key versions 1 and 2) plus the retiring estate's
  root-Store PDAs as a finalized devnet observation. Generated with solders
  (solana-program's Rust find_program_address); re-derived in the test by
  @solana/web3.js (chain-ix) and lib/solana-address.mjs; its seed layout is
  checked against every seeds = [...] of the four accounts in the program.
- example profile SAN is store.sidecar.host.

Mutation controls run: restoring `${rootStoreId}-v2` (profile and closure),
approving `store` in two plan steps, ordering the manifest step first,
altering a seed in chain-ix, the program source or the vector, and removing
the SAN and u32 guards each fail by name.

